## Network Traffic Analysis – TryHackMe

I successfully completed the Network Traffic Basics room on TryHackMe, where I gained foundational skills in understanding and analyzing 
network communications.

## Topics Covered

  -Fundamentals of network traffic analysis
  -Importance of network monitoring in cybersecurity
  -Structure of network packets (MAC, IP, TCP/UDP, application layers)
  -DNS, HTTP, and common protocol behaviors
  -Identifying suspicious or malicious traffic patterns

## Tools Practiced

  -Wireshark for packet capture and inspection
  -Network taps and SPAN/mirror ports for traffic collection
  -Basic Linux networking utilities for traffic observation

## Techniques Learned

  -Capturing and filtering network traffic efficiently
  -Inspecting packet structure across multiple OSI layers
  -Following TCP/UDP streams to reconstruct communication flows
  -Identifying key indicators within DNS and HTTP traffic
  -Extracting meaningful insights from raw packet data

## Key Takeaway

This lab strengthened my understanding of how network communication works at a packet level and how attackers can be detected through 
careful traffic analysis.
